// Base build configuration for the Namespace app target.
//
// Signing: by default the app signs ad-hoc ("Sign to Run Locally"). That's fine for
// contributors and CI — no setup required, and this file is a no-op for them.
//
// Running ./setup-signing.sh creates a stable self-signed certificate and writes
// Signing.local.xcconfig (git-ignored). The optional include at the bottom picks it up,
// overriding the settings here so every Xcode rebuild produces the SAME code signature.
// macOS TCC keys Accessibility / Automation grants on that signature, so your grants then
// survive rebuilds instead of being invalidated each time.
//
// The `?` in `#include?` makes the include optional: if the local file is absent, this
// line is silently skipped and the ad-hoc default below stands.

CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
